            <div xml:id="d792">

                <pb facs="1002" n="900" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg900"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/3008a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-12-09T18:00:00-05:00">December 9, 1935—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>145. An Associated Press despatch from Addis Ababa states that representatives of
                    the International Red Cross there have sent a formal protest to the League
                    concerning the bombing of the American Seventh Day Adventist hospital at Dessye.
                    A Reuters despatch from the same place states merely that seven doctors there
                    have executed an affidavit concerning the bombing. A United Press despatch
                    states that seven doctors have issued a formal protest.</p>
                <p>Please telegraph any pertinent information available in Geneva, also whether
                    International Red Cross authorities there recognize that hospital as being
                    affiliated with their organization.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
